1489:// hint (Project.Region carries no per-cluster meaning once one project spans
1540:		Region:    jurisdiction,
1659:		p.ID, p.Name, p.OwnerType, p.OwnerID, p.Region,
---
// ownerType is "org" (org-owned upstream → the COR-432 linked org) or "account"
// (user-owned upstream → the owning GitHub user's Entire account). The project
// gets the standard ProjectCreated authz shape for that owner type: org-owned is
// member-less so only a platform admin resolves manage (via platform->admin);
// account-owned bundles the owner's writer grant per the usual convention.
// entire-core writes repos and grants under it by writing tuples directly,
// never by holding a role.
//
// jurisdiction seeds Project.Region on first create only — a non-enforced
// hint (Project.Region carries no per-cluster meaning once one project spans
// every cluster an owner mirrors into) that simply reflects whichever
// cluster's mirror-create won the race to mint the project. No
// system_managed flag: a mirrors project holding repos is already
// undeletable (DeleteProject refuses on ErrHasRepos), and an empty one is
// harmless — this call re-mints it.
//
// Idempotent under concurrency: the loser of a create race re-reads and
// returns the winner's project. created reports whether this call minted it.
// The find paths do NOT re-assert the authz tuples: every mirror create ends
// in regional.RegisterMirrorAsNativeRepo, whose batched SpiceDB write TOUCHes
// the project's system tuples (authz.MirrorPlacementRegistered), so a project
