157	<header class="hero">
158	  <p class="eyebrow">Direction · Trails</p>
159	  <h1>Trails, Reshaped</h1>
160	  <p class="lede">A trail becomes the <strong>coordination artifact</strong>: one piece of intent that can span several changes, several repos, and several forges. The thing you review and ship today doesn't go away — it becomes the trail's member unit, working title <strong>change request</strong>.</p>
161	  <p class="muted">Summary of the direction for discussion. Details live in the design spec; this page is deliberately the high-level shape.</p>
162	</header>
163	
164	<section>
165	  <p class="eyebrow">The model</p>
166	  <h2>One trail, many changes</h2>
167	  <p>Today one trail is one change — one branch, at most one PR. That's the wrong altitude for intent: real work is a feature across repos, a stack of dependent changes, or an epic with children. The split:</p>
